WEBVTT


00:00:25.800 --> 00:00:31.158
Tuesday, After Christmas


00:01:27.396 --> 00:01:29.465
- It's really off.
- What is?


00:01:30.115 --> 00:01:31.594
Can't you see?


00:01:32.595 --> 00:01:34.347
It's ugly.


00:01:35.395 --> 00:01:38.068
Normally, one has a big one, a
smaller one and an even smaller one.


00:01:39.435 --> 00:01:40.788
Beautiful.


00:01:40.995 --> 00:01:42.905
Aesthetically pleasing.


00:01:44.234 --> 00:01:46.429
Wherever did I find you, you aesthete?


00:01:47.034 --> 00:01:49.343
Wherever did I find you,
with these mutant toes?!


00:01:49.554 --> 00:01:52.352
You're clueless. This is a sign,
of virility in men.


00:01:52.874 --> 00:01:54.512
So what is it in women?


00:01:56.074 --> 00:01:58.143
Still a sign of virility.


00:01:59.153 --> 00:02:00.871
So, see? I'm right.


00:02:01.673 --> 00:02:03.982
As a woman, I'm better off without.


00:02:06.633 --> 00:02:10.421
Your index toe is the mark of
an artistic temperament.


00:02:11.072 --> 00:02:12.710
Of the creator type.


00:02:13.232 --> 00:02:15.871
I don't know, in my book,
it's a sign I've got a big dick.


00:02:16.512 --> 00:02:18.389
I've seen bigger.


00:02:21.352 --> 00:02:23.308
Wherever did you see
such big ones?


00:02:23.992 --> 00:02:26.744
Back home, on the beach,
in Constanta.


00:02:27.551 --> 00:02:29.030
So did you see them, too?


00:02:29.231 --> 00:02:30.550
"Yeah!"


00:02:30.751 --> 00:02:31.951
What ever did you see?


00:02:32.071 --> 00:02:35.507
- "Big dicks!"
- You chatterbox, you!


00:02:35.711 --> 00:02:37.224
Yes, mutant.


00:02:38.990 --> 00:02:40.343
Let me see...


00:02:46.030 --> 00:02:48.021
Paula, quit your smoking, Paula!


00:02:48.550 --> 00:02:50.859
Oh, right you are. C'mon,
let me have a smoke.


00:02:51.390 --> 00:02:53.300
- Just one ciggie, babe!
- No...


00:02:55.709 --> 00:02:57.347
Why are you upsetting me?


00:02:58.029 --> 00:02:59.701
Can't you see what it does,
to your teeth?


00:03:00.029 --> 00:03:02.099
Don't you call me in for a,
plaque removal. I'm not coming.


00:03:02.429 --> 00:03:04.420
If you keep smoking like a mad man...


00:03:05.669 --> 00:03:08.785
- Oh, no. I just had one. No.
- What do you mean you just had one?


00:03:08.988 --> 00:03:11.582
Should be about 4 months now. Five.


00:03:11.868 --> 00:03:15.178
- We'll do it next time you bring Mara.
- You've already taken her measurements.


00:03:15.628 --> 00:03:17.459
Give me the braces, and we're through.


00:03:17.788 --> 00:03:19.585
Don't change the topic.


00:03:20.548 --> 00:03:22.663
Promise me you'll quit on Christmas.


00:03:24.027 --> 00:03:25.346
As a present...


00:03:26.387 --> 00:03:27.820
For your gal.


00:03:28.827 --> 00:03:30.624
What's smoking got to do
with Christmas?


00:03:31.027 --> 00:03:33.018
I told you I just can't do it.


00:03:33.667 --> 00:03:35.418
Come on, love... How come I did it?


00:03:35.866 --> 00:03:37.584
Well, I just can't.


00:03:39.186 --> 00:03:42.576
I'll ask Santa to bring me
a man with more willpower.


00:03:43.186 --> 00:03:44.460
Go ahead.


00:03:45.106 --> 00:03:47.301
Hasn't anybody told you that
he doesn't exist?


00:03:48.666 --> 00:03:51.623
I don't know. He came by my place
and left a present for you.


00:03:53.945 --> 00:03:55.617
- Oh, really?
- Yeah.


00:03:56.265 --> 00:03:59.894
- It's 'cause I've been a good boy
- You haven't been all that good.


00:04:00.825 --> 00:04:02.975
You've tricked Santa this year.


00:04:12.464 --> 00:04:14.056
I didn't get anything for my mom.


00:04:15.104 --> 00:04:17.412
- Never mind, there's still time.
- Not really.


00:04:17.623 --> 00:04:19.853
Her birthday is
the day after tomorrow.


00:04:20.143 --> 00:04:21.343
Damn, that's right.


00:04:21.903 --> 00:04:23.575
Many happy returns.


00:04:23.783 --> 00:04:25.102
Thanks.


00:04:25.943 --> 00:04:27.535
So you're going and leaving me alone.


00:04:27.983 --> 00:04:31.054
Maybe something from Channel, to coax
her out of that Laura Biagiotti of hers.


00:04:31.782 --> 00:04:33.898
So you're going away
and leaving me alone, huh?


00:04:35.142 --> 00:04:36.734
Yeah, I'm leaving.


00:04:37.982 --> 00:04:39.859
I'm leaving 'cause I promised her, too.


00:04:40.222 --> 00:04:42.178
Do you know how long it's been
since I was last home?


00:04:42.422 --> 00:04:43.775
Weren't you there now, in October?


00:04:44.062 --> 00:04:46.575
How long did I stay? Barely two days.


00:04:47.461 --> 00:04:50.180
I came back quickly, 'cause you were
driving me crazy with your calls.


00:04:50.381 --> 00:04:52.656
Well, missing you was killing me!


00:04:53.101 --> 00:04:55.171
I know what was killing you...


00:04:55.781 --> 00:04:58.341
"Missing you... "


00:05:00.620 --> 00:05:01.848
You Celentano!


00:05:02.300 --> 00:05:04.416
I've got an Italian version, too.


00:05:04.820 --> 00:05:07.175
Oh, yeah? Let's hear it, then.


00:05:16.179 --> 00:05:18.693
I'm not in the italian mood today..


00:05:20.699 --> 00:05:22.098
What are you getting Mara?


00:05:22.299 --> 00:05:23.971
We were thinking of a snowboard.


00:05:24.619 --> 00:05:26.894
For her to go down the slopes
with her old man.


00:05:28.098 --> 00:05:29.372
Very nice.


00:05:33.938 --> 00:05:36.213
Too bad you don't want me
to teach you.


00:05:37.338 --> 00:05:39.693
Yeah Paul, I'll come with you
to Kaprun.


00:05:41.137 --> 00:05:43.935
You tell Adriana that someone else
I will be joining you there.


00:05:44.217 --> 00:05:46.526
Maybe you can put an extra bed
in your room.


00:05:46.897 --> 00:05:48.455
Where do you think you're going?


00:05:53.337 --> 00:05:56.567
We can go to the mountains whenever
you want to. But you just don't.


00:05:56.976 --> 00:05:58.250
Yes, I do.


00:05:59.376 --> 00:06:00.650
You do?


00:06:01.176 --> 00:06:02.450
Yes.


00:06:03.376 --> 00:06:04.650
All right, then.


00:06:13.695 --> 00:06:15.128
No, please, don't.


00:06:15.535 --> 00:06:16.809
Really.


00:06:18.975 --> 00:06:21.694
Really now, open the windows, please...


00:06:23.174 --> 00:06:26.007
Come on, seriously!
Leave me alone, don't be a cow!


00:06:28.054 --> 00:06:29.282
No! Cut it out!


00:06:29.574 --> 00:06:31.565
Cut it out, I can't take it anymore!


00:06:37.373 --> 00:06:39.568
I told you to carpet this place.


00:06:44.813 --> 00:06:46.292
Lift me up.


00:06:52.132 --> 00:06:53.406
Rambo...


00:06:54.172 --> 00:06:56.606
I nearly broke my tailbone...


00:07:01.892 --> 00:07:03.564
I'm sitting up straight...


00:07:07.451 --> 00:07:09.521
No, seriously...
I'll slap you!


00:07:10.091 --> 00:07:12.241
I just wanted to give you this.
And I'm injured, too.


00:07:12.771 --> 00:07:14.124
Oh, good grief, you...


00:07:14.531 --> 00:07:15.930
You stupid cow.


00:07:17.091 --> 00:07:19.888
See what you did there? Huh?


00:07:31.130 --> 00:07:32.404
You latin lover...


00:07:32.730 --> 00:07:34.959
Hooch, give me my cigarettes, please.


00:07:40.009 --> 00:07:41.522
What're these?


00:07:41.729 --> 00:07:43.048
Your cigarettes.


00:07:59.848 --> 00:08:01.122
Paul...


00:08:01.367 --> 00:08:02.641
Paul!


00:08:03.287 --> 00:08:05.164
Come here for a second, please.


00:08:15.406 --> 00:08:17.362
- It's great.
- Isn't it?


00:08:18.286 --> 00:08:21.039
I'll go look for some shoes, too,
and that's it, Santa's come for me.


00:08:23.566 --> 00:08:25.796
I like this... patterned one.


00:08:26.326 --> 00:08:27.600
I want to get that one for my sis.


00:08:27.926 --> 00:08:29.563
It won't fit her. You get it.


00:08:29.765 --> 00:08:32.120
- You think?
- Definitely.


00:08:34.245 --> 00:08:36.520
It's a bit stretchy and it'll give.


00:08:42.885 --> 00:08:44.442
Well, we'll see...


00:08:44.724 --> 00:08:47.921
See? That's why it's better for you
to get stuff for yourself.


00:08:49.164 --> 00:08:50.995
I'll take it and we'll see.


00:08:54.564 --> 00:08:56.759
- Check these out, see if they fit.
- What's up with these?


00:08:57.124 --> 00:08:59.398
Your folks gave me some money
to get you new boots.


00:08:59.643 --> 00:09:01.634
Come on, Adriana,
what's with this nonsense?


00:09:01.843 --> 00:09:03.595
What do you want me to do Paul,
argue with them?


00:09:04.203 --> 00:09:05.921
Try them on, it won't kill you.


00:09:09.403 --> 00:09:11.870
Just be thankful they didn't buy
them themselves.


00:09:13.522 --> 00:09:14.796
Here, hold this.


00:09:16.722 --> 00:09:19.156
And please act surprised when
you get them.


00:09:19.722 --> 00:09:21.201
- Oh, I'll act up all right!
- That's the spirit!


00:09:21.402 --> 00:09:23.154
On the one hand we give them money,


00:09:23.362 --> 00:09:25.875
and they give it to us to get boots.


00:09:27.601 --> 00:09:28.829
Is this it?


00:09:29.121 --> 00:09:32.079
No. He's looking for a smaller one.


00:09:32.481 --> 00:09:34.756
This one's 130 and it's too long.


00:09:36.001 --> 00:09:37.957
It's got pink, she'll like it.


00:09:38.721 --> 00:09:40.756
Will we ever get out of this
pink phase?


00:09:42.160 --> 00:09:44.151
- Do they fit?
- Perfect!


00:09:44.680 --> 00:09:46.989
I can climb mountains now!


00:09:47.440 --> 00:09:49.158
Here, this is the only small board
we've got.


00:09:49.520 --> 00:09:50.919
And it's the last one.


00:09:53.559 --> 00:09:54.992
No. We'll keep looking.


00:09:55.199 --> 00:09:57.838
There's nowhere else to look.


00:09:58.319 --> 00:10:01.436
It's the only place left with kid's boards.


00:10:04.039 --> 00:10:05.267
We'll give it some more thought.


00:10:05.479 --> 00:10:07.276
OK, you call me...


00:10:09.318 --> 00:10:11.434
Then let's get her one from Austria.


00:10:11.718 --> 00:10:14.232
- We'll find her another gift for now.
- What else?


00:10:14.438 --> 00:10:16.235
I don't know, we'll look around.


00:10:16.478 --> 00:10:17.991
Girlie, we're not going to look for
anything else.


00:10:18.358 --> 00:10:19.791
Seriously, what else?


00:10:19.998 --> 00:10:22.067
We said we'd get her a board,
let's get her a board!


00:10:22.477 --> 00:10:24.195
She even wrote Santa about it.


00:10:24.797 --> 00:10:26.708
- We can't just change our minds.
- I'm not going to put


00:10:26.917 --> 00:10:28.908
a skeleton board
under the Christmas tree.


00:10:31.477 --> 00:10:32.705
Yes...


00:10:33.717 --> 00:10:36.867
I'm very impressed...
What did the guy tell you?


00:10:39.876 --> 00:10:42.515
But I never told him there was
a fixed interest rate.


00:10:43.356 --> 00:10:44.869
Man, does this guy think
we're all morons?!


00:10:45.076 --> 00:10:46.276
He should thank the bank.


00:10:47.316 --> 00:10:48.795
Show him the file.


00:10:51.155 --> 00:10:53.305
Don't these people ever watch TV?


00:10:56.635 --> 00:10:59.069
No, you're going to take the file
from Carmen and go over to him.


00:11:00.275 --> 00:11:01.947
She will give it to you.


00:11:06.754 --> 00:11:09.473
Well, what could I tell him
that you couldn't?


00:11:12.474 --> 00:11:13.827
All right, forget it.


00:11:14.274 --> 00:11:17.072
Tell him I'll stop by his place
and talk to him.


00:11:18.673 --> 00:11:21.187
Yeah... thank you so much
for you help...


00:11:21.433 --> 00:11:22.707
Come on, bye.


00:11:25.153 --> 00:11:26.381
So?


00:11:27.313 --> 00:11:29.383
We'll just have to get this pink one.


00:11:29.793 --> 00:11:31.589
We'll drop it off at my parents'.


00:11:31.792 --> 00:11:32.992
All right.


00:11:33.032 --> 00:11:35.546
And if it's too tall,
it'll fit her next year.


00:11:35.912 --> 00:11:38.745
It'll just be a bit tougher for her
to steer.


00:11:39.112 --> 00:11:40.784
But she'll get used to it.


00:11:42.352 --> 00:11:43.626
You like 'em?


00:11:44.512 --> 00:11:46.024
I'm smitten.


00:12:03.830 --> 00:12:05.149
- Where's mommy?
- She's on the phone


00:12:05.350 --> 00:12:07.147
with... Salrom.


00:12:07.350 --> 00:12:09.068
With "Salrrrom"?


00:12:10.590 --> 00:12:13.979
File no. 7. 800. 077


00:12:14.309 --> 00:12:16.459
regarding Court ruling


00:12:16.829 --> 00:12:18.945
no. 1.000. 200. 077


00:12:20.429 --> 00:12:22.181
- Careful, you'll break it like this.
- No, I won't!


00:12:22.389 --> 00:12:23.663
- Yes, you will...
- No, I won't.


00:12:24.829 --> 00:12:26.706
I told you we'd open a can of worms.


00:12:27.109 --> 00:12:28.382
Meaning?


00:12:29.028 --> 00:12:31.303
Will she take him out and feed him?


00:12:31.868 --> 00:12:33.142
It's out of the question.


00:12:33.708 --> 00:12:35.744
That's what I told her, too.


00:12:36.988 --> 00:12:38.979
Santa won't bring her another pet.


00:12:39.388 --> 00:12:42.060
She already has Coco
and she needs to take care of him.


00:12:42.787 --> 00:12:45.062
So then why do you give me
the "meaning" routine?


00:12:46.147 --> 00:12:48.707
Anyway, this Santa business won't
hold out for much longer.


00:12:49.027 --> 00:12:50.824
- Mommins!
- Yes, honey!


00:12:51.187 --> 00:12:53.143
We're out of liquid soap!


00:12:53.707 --> 00:12:56.664
OK, honey. Use the regular one.


00:12:58.186 --> 00:13:00.142
- Is there any left?
- Yes.


00:13:01.906 --> 00:13:04.864
She doesn't believes that
Santa gets her letters.


00:13:05.226 --> 00:13:07.217
Last year she wanted a talking parrot


00:13:07.466 --> 00:13:08.979
and Coco just cackles.


00:13:09.306 --> 00:13:11.455
Santa's not what he used to be...


00:13:12.945 --> 00:13:14.822
What were you talking about?


00:13:15.185 --> 00:13:16.937
I was just telling mom about a movie.


00:13:17.825 --> 00:13:19.258
What kind of movie?


00:13:20.145 --> 00:13:21.817
A movie for grown-ups.


00:13:22.305 --> 00:13:23.579
OK then...


00:13:23.904 --> 00:13:25.542
If you don't tell me,


00:13:25.864 --> 00:13:28.094
I won't tell you other stuff either.


00:13:28.504 --> 00:13:30.142
What other stuff?


00:13:30.704 --> 00:13:31.978
Nothing...


00:13:32.824 --> 00:13:35.338
-Do you have something to tell us?
- No.


00:13:35.704 --> 00:13:37.456
- Are you sure?
- I'm sure.


00:13:38.063 --> 00:13:39.815
Then start eating and shut up.


00:13:40.103 --> 00:13:41.377
- Did you wash your hands?
-Yes.


00:13:41.703 --> 00:13:42.931
Let me see.


00:13:53.182 --> 00:13:54.979
What's with the grass?


00:13:55.902 --> 00:13:58.735
I'm not a giraffe,
I won't eat this thing.


00:13:59.062 --> 00:14:00.415
No, you're a goat, not a giraffe...


00:14:00.702 --> 00:14:01.930
Not even that...


00:14:04.302 --> 00:14:07.691
See, I put in some spinach for you...
rocket salad...


00:14:08.461 --> 00:14:10.053
Come on, eat. Please.


00:14:10.861 --> 00:14:12.897
I'd rather have a cream cheese sandwich.


00:14:13.301 --> 00:14:15.417
Make yourself a cheese sandwich,
there isn't any left anyway...


00:14:15.741 --> 00:14:18.255
- Oh, give me a break...
- Make one with butter.


00:14:19.261 --> 00:14:20.739
Cream cheese is better.


00:14:23.740 --> 00:14:25.298
You want some cheese?


00:14:26.620 --> 00:14:27.894
Yes.


00:14:37.339 --> 00:14:40.376
I was thinking of buying
a Christmas present for Mara.


00:14:40.739 --> 00:14:42.013
Why?


00:14:42.219 --> 00:14:43.811
That's what I'd like to do.


00:14:44.219 --> 00:14:46.892
I could give it to her at the clinic.
That way it won't cause any trouble.


00:14:48.298 --> 00:14:51.256
- Well, no. What's the point
- Why?


00:14:51.778 --> 00:14:54.451
It's not about the trouble. It just,
doesn't make any sense for now.


00:14:55.258 --> 00:14:57.294
It's my pleasure.


00:14:57.938 --> 00:14:59.974
There'll be plenty of opportunities.


00:15:00.818 --> 00:15:02.091
Whatever...


00:15:05.377 --> 00:15:07.766
- Do you think it's inappropriate?
- What is?


00:15:09.017 --> 00:15:11.167
- This present thing.
- God forbid.


00:15:16.976 --> 00:15:19.968
Because if you don't agree,
I'll do whatever you tell me to.


00:15:21.256 --> 00:15:22.689
You get to have the last say.


00:15:23.016 --> 00:15:24.688
Don't worry about it.


00:15:33.295 --> 00:15:35.047
Then you give them to her.


00:15:35.735 --> 00:15:38.090
I hope she likes them
and I hope they fit.


00:15:38.655 --> 00:15:40.566
Wow, they're awesome!


00:15:41.135 --> 00:15:44.171
I'll have you know I asked around,
I didn't just wing it.


00:15:48.014 --> 00:15:49.970
Let me kiss you for her.


00:15:50.174 --> 00:15:51.766
Thank you, Santa!


00:15:52.214 --> 00:15:53.966
Don't forget to put them
under the Christmas tree.


00:15:54.894 --> 00:15:56.885
They've got some pink, too...


00:15:57.773 --> 00:15:59.047
Real cool.


00:16:05.173 --> 00:16:06.572
Are you staying on for lunch?


00:16:06.773 --> 00:16:08.650
No. I've got to split.


00:16:10.053 --> 00:16:11.883
- Is it four o'clock already?
-Yes.


00:16:13.532 --> 00:16:15.488
Hurry on home
to the wife and kids, then.


00:16:15.892 --> 00:16:17.166
Am I interfering with your schedule?


00:16:17.852 --> 00:16:19.365
Why wouldn't you, Paul?


00:16:19.572 --> 00:16:22.211
- Single woman, beautiful...
- Who is it?


00:16:23.092 --> 00:16:26.322
Don't you worry, there are always
a couple of guys warming up.


00:16:27.171 --> 00:16:29.127
Well, introduce me to them, then.


00:16:29.451 --> 00:16:30.930
Next time I get the chance.


00:16:31.131 --> 00:16:32.405
By all means.


00:16:41.850 --> 00:16:43.329
That's it, then...


00:16:49.090 --> 00:16:51.650
- What's that?
- Santa's come to our place, too.


00:17:01.169 --> 00:17:02.397
Why do you do stuff like this?


00:17:02.609 --> 00:17:04.486
- What?
- You know I can't go.


00:17:05.849 --> 00:17:07.521
Why? They're for the 23rd.


00:17:07.729 --> 00:17:09.002
Yes, Paul. They're for the 23rd.


00:17:09.208 --> 00:17:11.324
I'll be in Constanta on the 23rd.


00:17:11.728 --> 00:17:13.684
Well, didn't you say you were going
to go there now, for her birthday?


00:17:14.048 --> 00:17:16.926
So what am I going to do, Paul, mess
around on the road on Christmas Eve?


00:17:17.288 --> 00:17:18.562
I can't.


00:17:19.648 --> 00:17:22.207
This is the kind of thing I'd rather
we decided upon together.


00:17:22.447 --> 00:17:25.439
Yeah, OK, make a big fuss 'cause I
got you a couple of concert tickets.


00:17:25.847 --> 00:17:29.157
- I thought I'd surprise you.
- You'd better not start with this.


00:17:29.887 --> 00:17:32.799
You don't want to, we won't go
and that's that. Big deal.


00:17:35.167 --> 00:17:36.804
But it's a shame, though...


00:17:39.126 --> 00:17:40.878
You're something else...


00:17:42.646 --> 00:17:44.557
C'mon, scram!


00:17:45.366 --> 00:17:46.640
I'll see you tomorrow.


00:17:47.086 --> 00:17:48.724
Tomorrow's the last time
I see you this year.


00:17:49.126 --> 00:17:50.877
Good thing I'll be rid of you.


00:17:51.245 --> 00:17:52.803
Rid of me...


00:18:04.204 --> 00:18:05.717
I forgot...


00:18:33.962 --> 00:18:37.113
- So why did you two argue?
- Because she stole my cow pen.


00:18:38.642 --> 00:18:41.110
- But are you sure she stole it?
- Yeah.


00:18:41.322 --> 00:18:46.111
Because mine used to keep jamming and
then the next day she wrote with it.


00:18:46.321 --> 00:18:49.119
And it kept jamming. Just like mine.


00:18:50.881 --> 00:18:53.270
And she said it was brand new.


00:18:53.721 --> 00:18:55.598
But I know she took it from me.


00:18:56.121 --> 00:18:57.679
Come on, now, quit pouting.


00:18:58.161 --> 00:19:00.390
I didn't like this Alexia anyway.


00:19:00.840 --> 00:19:02.910
She's mean and she's a jerk.


00:19:03.720 --> 00:19:04.948
Mind your language.


00:19:05.240 --> 00:19:07.993
I even moved out of our desk.
Let her share a desk with Steffi.


00:19:08.840 --> 00:19:10.831
- Are the two of them friends now?
- Yeah...


00:19:11.080 --> 00:19:13.469
And they keep saying
gross stuff about me.


00:19:13.840 --> 00:19:15.750
She's very mean and a big jerk, too...


00:19:16.159 --> 00:19:17.990
I told you to mind your language.


00:19:18.839 --> 00:19:20.511
So, with whom do you share your desk?


00:19:21.479 --> 00:19:24.391
- With Bogdan Dema.
- With whom?


00:19:24.599 --> 00:19:26.078
With Bogdan Dema.


00:19:27.159 --> 00:19:28.511
Is that the one who...


00:19:29.318 --> 00:19:31.229
Is that the one who was
at your birthday...


00:19:31.598 --> 00:19:33.987
-... and did the cake thing?
- No... He's this new kid.


00:19:34.438 --> 00:19:36.315
- Oh, so it's a different kid?
- Yeah.


00:19:39.118 --> 00:19:41.632
So what kind of gross things
are they saying about you?


00:19:42.517 --> 00:19:46.795
That I cheat on the math tests,
and that I eat boogers, and stuff...


00:19:51.677 --> 00:19:52.951
Yes, Mom.


00:19:53.237 --> 00:19:54.465
What are you two doing?


00:19:54.877 --> 00:19:57.788
We just left school and we're
on our way to get the x-ray.


00:19:59.316 --> 00:20:00.544
You?


00:20:00.916 --> 00:20:03.908
Well, the bailiffs are on strike,
so we've all gone home.


00:20:04.716 --> 00:20:06.752
So they just went on strike,
without any sort of notice?


00:20:07.516 --> 00:20:09.905
Yeah. At a quarter to two,
with a full courtroom.


00:20:10.155 --> 00:20:11.383
You tell me...


00:20:12.635 --> 00:20:14.591
So what are you going to do now,
hit the gym?


00:20:15.195 --> 00:20:17.550
No, I was thinking to join you
at the dentist's office,


00:20:17.875 --> 00:20:20.025
and then we could all go
to your parents' place.


00:20:21.155 --> 00:20:23.111
How are you doing there, sweetie?
Are you nervous, baby?


00:20:23.315 --> 00:20:25.191
Are you coming with us, too, Mom?


00:20:25.394 --> 00:20:27.544
I sure am.
To see how brave you are.


00:20:27.754 --> 00:20:30.552
But I don't think she's going to get
her braces put in today.


00:20:31.194 --> 00:20:32.273
That's what you told me.


00:20:32.274 --> 00:20:34.185
No, I said I was going over
to the dentist's, but...


00:20:34.474 --> 00:20:36.305
I don't know the exact procedure
for today.


00:20:37.514 --> 00:20:38.992
Yes... We'll see.


00:20:41.153 --> 00:20:44.384
As you wish, but we can stop by
afterwards and pick you up from home.


00:20:45.393 --> 00:20:47.668
No, it's all right, I'll join you.


00:20:48.033 --> 00:20:49.671
Tell me the exact address.


00:20:51.233 --> 00:20:54.429
I don't think there's any point...
It's behind Hala Traian.


00:20:56.192 --> 00:20:58.831
It's this old, four-storied building.
Popa Soare 45.


00:21:01.072 --> 00:21:02.983
OK, I got it.


00:21:04.112 --> 00:21:06.909
Don't rush. We'll get there in
about an hour or so.


00:21:07.831 --> 00:21:09.469
All right, then... See you there.


00:21:10.951 --> 00:21:12.942
- Kisses, you two!
- Bye-bye.


00:21:13.471 --> 00:21:15.985
- Bye, Mom.
- Bye-bye, baby...


00:21:29.830 --> 00:21:31.104
Mommy!


00:21:31.430 --> 00:21:32.863
- Hey! How's it going, princess?
- I brought in the x-rays!


00:21:33.150 --> 00:21:35.265
- You're here already.
- Yeah. I got here five minutes ago.


00:21:35.829 --> 00:21:37.029
Look at those nice pictures...


00:21:37.349 --> 00:21:40.546
- Look how good I look here!
- Yeah... You're gorgeous.


00:21:41.109 --> 00:21:42.309
Did you have a hard time
finding the place?


00:21:42.389 --> 00:21:45.062
No, not at all. I know the area,
I sometimes drop by to see Jeni.


00:21:45.829 --> 00:21:48.581
- So her office is around here.
- Right next to the restaurant.


00:21:50.228 --> 00:21:52.822
Oh, look, baby, your hair looks
really great in this one.


00:21:54.268 --> 00:21:56.418
Oh my God, what crocodile did
they take a picture of here?


00:21:56.628 --> 00:21:58.186
Oh, my, you gave me such a fright!


00:21:59.548 --> 00:22:01.584
- How are you?
- I'm beat...


00:22:03.227 --> 00:22:06.185
- Did you talk to them?
- Yeah, she's got someone inside.


00:22:06.867 --> 00:22:09.335
So, tell me, baby...
Were you scared?


00:22:09.707 --> 00:22:13.382
No. They put this thing on my
forehead, for a couple of times.


00:22:14.427 --> 00:22:17.577
Then they put this other thing
on my nose, like a sort of laser...


00:22:18.106 --> 00:22:19.459
and then they put a vest on me, see?


00:22:19.866 --> 00:22:21.663
And it was too heavy,


00:22:22.026 --> 00:22:24.824
So I sat down on a chair.


00:22:25.746 --> 00:22:28.897
Then they put these plastic
spoons in my mouth...


00:22:30.625 --> 00:22:32.900
Oh, Mr. Hanganu, the pleasure.


00:22:33.265 --> 00:22:34.584
Did you bring the patient in?


00:22:34.825 --> 00:22:36.224
Let me introduce you to my wife.


00:22:36.425 --> 00:22:39.098
- Adriana Hanganu.
- Mircea Dumbraveanu, glad to meet you.


00:22:39.385 --> 00:22:40.613
You know Mara.


00:22:41.065 --> 00:22:42.657
- Sure I do. How's it going, Missy?
- Fine.


00:22:43.025 --> 00:22:44.582
"Fine". Brief and to the point.


00:22:45.024 --> 00:22:46.901
That's how she usually communicates.


00:22:48.304 --> 00:22:50.613
- Mommy, let me show you something!
- Please excuse me.


00:22:53.104 --> 00:22:54.822
I can't really tell who she looks like.


00:22:55.104 --> 00:22:57.334
She's taken after both of us,
so that we don't get upset.


00:22:57.544 --> 00:22:59.295
She's real cute...


00:22:59.983 --> 00:23:02.338
- How you doin', man?
- Working, what else?


00:23:02.663 --> 00:23:05.131
I'm staying on to help Raluca,
Marcela had to go earlier.


00:23:06.823 --> 00:23:08.051
How's the house doing?


00:23:08.383 --> 00:23:09.975
The house is the problem.


00:23:10.183 --> 00:23:13.697
I mean, I've built it,
I've put up the roof...


00:23:13.902 --> 00:23:16.291
But that's it.
The money pipe stopped running.


00:23:16.582 --> 00:23:18.573
- You've exceeded your budget.
- Really bad.


00:23:18.782 --> 00:23:20.977
So what can you do?
Just be patient...


00:23:21.342 --> 00:23:23.412
I might pay you a visit after all.


00:23:23.902 --> 00:23:25.540
Maybe you can help me scrape up
another line of credit.


00:23:25.822 --> 00:23:27.891
- You got the first one from...
- From BRD.


00:23:28.861 --> 00:23:30.340
- What, is there anything wrong?
- No, it's all right...


00:23:31.501 --> 00:23:33.412
It'll be one year this January.


00:23:34.981 --> 00:23:37.449
Then, I'll be expecting you.


00:23:38.061 --> 00:23:40.335
Bring the paperwork for your loan.


00:23:41.100 --> 00:23:43.534
I don't want to take out another loan
but I don't have a choice.


00:23:43.900 --> 00:23:45.333
This house knocked me out...


00:23:45.820 --> 00:23:47.173
Look who's here...


00:23:47.460 --> 00:23:49.815
- How are you, pretty girl?
- Fine.


00:23:50.180 --> 00:23:51.339
- Hello.
- Hello.


00:23:51.340 --> 00:23:53.774
- How are you?
- With the patient...


00:23:54.180 --> 00:23:56.135
Very nice. Come on in please.


00:23:56.579 --> 00:23:58.297
I'll be there in a second.


00:24:00.939 --> 00:24:02.770
- Did you bring the file, too?
- Yes.


00:24:03.539 --> 00:24:04.892
Mara, where'd you put the file?


00:24:05.339 --> 00:24:06.931
Oopsie! It's on the table.


00:24:17.218 --> 00:24:19.049
Can I take that laser gun?


00:24:20.058 --> 00:24:21.571
A bit later.


00:24:24.297 --> 00:24:26.128
You can ask Daddy to make you ride
the elevator a bit, if you want to.


00:24:26.697 --> 00:24:28.449
Yeah! Please, Daddy, will you?


00:24:30.657 --> 00:24:32.648
Just a bit. We don't want
to break anything...


00:24:33.737 --> 00:24:35.932
Oh... This is so great!
I can even go to sleep.


00:24:41.936 --> 00:24:43.654
We'll leave you here.


00:24:44.456 --> 00:24:45.684
That's enough.


00:24:46.936 --> 00:24:49.609
It's morning already!


00:24:50.056 --> 00:24:53.127
I don't know if you're up to speed
with Mara's issues.


00:24:53.335 --> 00:24:54.414
Sort of...


00:24:54.415 --> 00:24:57.168
- Or how much Mr. Hanganu told you.
- He's told me some things.


00:24:57.375 --> 00:24:58.649
As much as I could remember.


00:24:59.095 --> 00:25:01.086
I'll run you through the whole thing
once again, then.


00:25:09.014 --> 00:25:11.653
Mara's got a slight under-bite.


00:25:26.333 --> 00:25:27.732
That's it...


00:25:28.413 --> 00:25:29.846
Come closer, please.


00:25:30.533 --> 00:25:31.761
Close it.


00:25:32.213 --> 00:25:35.045
This is particularly apparent
if you look at the molar teeth.


00:25:35.572 --> 00:25:37.403
Those are the first
permanent molars...


00:25:38.932 --> 00:25:40.843
...to emerge behind the baby teeth.


00:25:41.212 --> 00:25:43.328
She hasn't gotten all
her permanent teeth yet.


00:25:43.772 --> 00:25:45.842
We don't know how the other ones
will evolve...


00:25:46.212 --> 00:25:48.771
but this is the mark of
a slight maxillary pressure


00:25:49.451 --> 00:25:51.840
...the narrowing of the upper arch bone.


00:25:52.931 --> 00:25:57.083
Her skeletal pattern is graded 3.
She has a slightly jutting mandible.


00:25:57.291 --> 00:26:00.169
- But I'm in the fourth grade...
- Good for you.


00:26:00.690 --> 00:26:03.363
Mara... let's see what the doctor
has to say, all right?


00:26:03.810 --> 00:26:05.038
Bottom line...


00:26:05.410 --> 00:26:07.401
Her superior arch bone is
insufficiently developed.


00:26:07.690 --> 00:26:09.043
It needs to be stimulated...


00:26:09.410 --> 00:26:12.163
...or her permanent teeth
will have no room.


00:26:12.890 --> 00:26:15.244
I'm talking about her canines.
Please close it a bit, Mara.


00:26:15.849 --> 00:26:19.000
Right now, her canine teeth
will emerge in vestibular position.


00:26:19.569 --> 00:26:21.400
- They just jut forward like this...
- Yes.


00:26:22.129 --> 00:26:24.006
These canine teeth are small...


00:26:24.289 --> 00:26:27.326
She'll get a bigger set of canines,


00:26:27.729 --> 00:26:30.447
- which will have no room to develop.
- But I won't get them now, am I?


00:26:30.968 --> 00:26:33.163
No. When you get slightly older.


00:26:33.648 --> 00:26:35.559
So, if we intervene now,


00:26:35.808 --> 00:26:37.685
we can automatically solve the issues


00:26:38.008 --> 00:26:40.397
with her entire upper arch...


00:26:40.608 --> 00:26:43.246
- Excuse me.
- Of course.


00:26:45.047 --> 00:26:47.163
Can I have the colored sheet?


00:26:47.767 --> 00:26:50.201
- What did you say?
- That paper with the colored bears.


00:26:51.327 --> 00:26:52.806
The colored bears...


00:26:55.967 --> 00:26:57.445
They should be around here...


00:26:57.846 --> 00:27:00.235
I had another girl in here earlier.


00:27:04.486 --> 00:27:05.839
Here you go.


00:27:08.086 --> 00:27:10.553
I knew there was a pink one, too!


00:27:11.005 --> 00:27:14.361
- Take your time looking.
- Dad, should I get a dark pink?


00:27:15.485 --> 00:27:16.918
I say purple.


00:27:17.165 --> 00:27:18.883
Nope... Pink!


00:27:20.565 --> 00:27:23.443
- What are you looking for?
- The removable braces...


00:27:23.645 --> 00:27:25.362
I'll go check in the other room.


00:27:28.444 --> 00:27:31.083
- I found them.
- Should I fix you some molding?


00:27:31.724 --> 00:27:33.874
Not right now. A bit later.


00:27:44.203 --> 00:27:45.602
I'm sorry.


00:27:45.883 --> 00:27:47.202
Don't worry about it.


00:27:48.443 --> 00:27:51.241
So, long story short, it's too early
for fixed braces.


00:27:51.643 --> 00:27:54.031
We don't have all
our permanent teeth yet,


00:27:54.362 --> 00:27:56.557
so we'll put her
a pair of removable braces.


00:27:56.762 --> 00:27:58.354
This is a sample...


00:27:59.442 --> 00:28:02.115
It's not a new piece, but an example
of what we're talking about.


00:28:02.642 --> 00:28:05.110
- I hope it turns out to be efficient.
- I think it will.


00:28:05.642 --> 00:28:08.394
Removable braces can stimulate
transversal development.


00:28:09.361 --> 00:28:12.353
- It was supposed to be pink!
- Your braces are going to be pink.


00:28:13.761 --> 00:28:15.240
I want a pink one...


00:28:15.881 --> 00:28:19.669
We've got plenty of time,
I believe that it will prove efficient.


00:28:20.600 --> 00:28:24.309
Later we might put in a spacer,
if we need...


00:28:24.520 --> 00:28:26.238
What's a spacer?


00:28:26.440 --> 00:28:29.238
- The spacer is the metallic butterfly.
- That really ugly one?


00:28:29.560 --> 00:28:31.676
The ugly one, yes.
I showed you last time.


00:28:34.240 --> 00:28:36.275
So how long does she have to wear it?


00:28:37.519 --> 00:28:39.350
At least sixteen hours a day.


00:28:39.679 --> 00:28:42.113
Wearing it at night alone
will not suffice.


00:28:42.599 --> 00:28:45.671
Teeth have a natural tendency of
resuming their initial positioning.


00:28:46.359 --> 00:28:48.747
I was actually asking for how long
will she need to wear it.


00:28:49.238 --> 00:28:51.593
- No longer than one year.
- That long?


00:28:52.838 --> 00:28:56.433
We could be looking at less time.
Her situation is not so complicated.


00:28:59.198 --> 00:29:02.076
It seems a bit too long, seeing as
it's not really necessary.


00:29:03.757 --> 00:29:05.827
I mean, it's not an emergency, is it?


00:29:06.837 --> 00:29:08.907
Well... It's not mandatory
or compulsory but...


00:29:09.517 --> 00:29:12.827
An under-bite can trigger
an abnormal development.


00:29:13.677 --> 00:29:16.066
Her facial bones
might develop asymmetrically.


00:29:17.596 --> 00:29:19.826
Obviously, it's your call.


00:29:20.916 --> 00:29:23.146
I don't want to torture her
if there's no point to it.


00:29:23.356 --> 00:29:25.551
- I'm telling you that there is a point.
- Mara.


00:29:26.276 --> 00:29:28.107
- Do you want to get those braces?
- Yes.


00:29:28.476 --> 00:29:29.795
- You do?
- Yes!


00:29:30.715 --> 00:29:32.751
- Can you keep wearing 'em for a year?
- Yes.


00:29:33.915 --> 00:29:35.951
- I don't want to hear any whining...
- Yes.


00:29:36.715 --> 00:29:38.910
Mara! You'll wear it,
as long as you need to.


00:29:39.675 --> 00:29:41.984
Even if some kid said
God-knows what.


00:29:42.195 --> 00:29:44.662
Yes, I'll wear it. I like it!


00:29:45.354 --> 00:29:46.582
She likes it.


00:29:51.754 --> 00:29:55.110
Anyway, from what the doctor's said,
she won't even feel it after a week.


00:29:55.834 --> 00:29:58.029
She will feel something,
it's only normal.


00:29:58.833 --> 00:30:02.109
But, as time goes by,
she'll get used.


00:30:02.793 --> 00:30:05.546
But she will have to wear it
nearly all day long.


00:30:09.873 --> 00:30:12.750
I say we should have it put in now.
We don't want things to complicate.


00:30:13.912 --> 00:30:15.470
Let's have it put in.


00:30:15.832 --> 00:30:18.585
- Whatever you say.
- You know best.


00:30:19.552 --> 00:30:21.747
Yes. Let's get to work then.


00:30:22.752 --> 00:30:24.583
Who is our next patient?


00:30:25.032 --> 00:30:27.261
Doctor, please take your seat...


00:30:28.791 --> 00:30:30.622
I am a doctor, too!


00:30:32.511 --> 00:30:35.423
We are going to get her dental
imprint for the braces now.


00:30:36.871 --> 00:30:39.624
It will be ready in a couple of days.
Before Christmas.


00:30:42.910 --> 00:30:45.185
One of you should bring Mara back in,


00:30:45.830 --> 00:30:48.708
to teach you how to adjust it.


00:30:50.030 --> 00:30:51.907
If I'm not here,
Mircea will show you what to do.


00:30:52.110 --> 00:30:55.465
- We'll adjust it ourselves?
- It's simple. With a little key.


00:30:58.229 --> 00:31:01.187
Well, I say we go out,
let the folks do their job.


00:31:02.429 --> 00:31:04.101
Can we stay here and watch, too?


00:31:04.589 --> 00:31:06.181
- Of course you can.
- Thanks.


00:31:10.828 --> 00:31:12.659
- Are you comfortable?
- Yes.


00:31:13.468 --> 00:31:15.299
Will I have a lisp?


00:31:15.668 --> 00:31:17.340
Not right now. In a couple of days.


00:31:17.788 --> 00:31:19.983
I'll test you with some spoons now.


00:31:20.308 --> 00:31:22.901
I need to know if anything hurts,
or feels awkward, OK?


00:31:23.107 --> 00:31:24.620
Are you going to talk like
Duffy Duck again?


00:31:24.827 --> 00:31:27.864
A bit later.
All right now, open wide...


00:31:28.507 --> 00:31:30.384
Is this all right?


00:31:31.387 --> 00:31:33.423
Good girl. Open wide, now.


00:31:40.746 --> 00:31:42.304
Why do you keep slamming it?


00:31:42.746 --> 00:31:44.782
I've told you a thousand times.
Like this.


00:31:45.346 --> 00:31:46.825
Look, nicely, like this.


00:31:50.586 --> 00:31:53.338
Please remind Ica to give you
the marbles, all right?


00:31:53.625 --> 00:31:55.741
- The yellow ones?
- The yellow ones tonight...


00:31:55.985 --> 00:31:58.294
...and the blue ones in the morning.
Until Monday.


00:31:58.745 --> 00:32:01.179
- Remind her, 'cause she forgets, OK?
- OK.


00:32:04.665 --> 00:32:08.134
No drinking, no eating for half
an hour before and after the marbles.


00:32:08.904 --> 00:32:10.417
All right. It's us!


00:32:11.024 --> 00:32:14.334
- You won't forget, will you?
- No, but Ica doesn't give them to me


00:32:14.544 --> 00:32:16.262
from the bottle cap,
but from her hand, not like you.


00:32:17.904 --> 00:32:19.894
- Well, let's talk to her.
- I've told her before,


00:32:20.103 --> 00:32:22.014
but she told me
that's the way to do it.


00:32:30.263 --> 00:32:32.697
This was '91,
when I got into college.


00:32:33.702 --> 00:32:36.057
I used to shave my head.


00:32:39.302 --> 00:32:40.815
I don't believe it!


00:32:41.142 --> 00:32:43.292
You were dating that guy,
the Timpuri Noi drummer, right?


00:32:43.702 --> 00:32:46.216
- No, we were already going out.
- I broke up with Tobi a year before.


00:32:48.621 --> 00:32:52.296
The punk! She used to change
her hair color every week.


00:32:53.181 --> 00:32:55.979
Timpuri Noi is the band that plays
that "Father" song, right?


00:32:58.581 --> 00:33:01.333
Come on, you guys, quit making
fun of me because I'm young.


00:33:03.780 --> 00:33:06.214
By the way, guys, did you know that
Enrique's dad is a singer, too?


00:33:07.340 --> 00:33:08.978
I heard a guy at the mall yesterday
telling another guy:


00:33:09.540 --> 00:33:12.179
"Did you know that Enrique's dad
is also a singer. "


00:33:15.699 --> 00:33:17.690
- But did you know?
- What?


00:33:17.899 --> 00:33:20.777
- That Enrique's dad...
- Enrique who?


00:33:23.019 --> 00:33:24.293
What?


00:33:26.659 --> 00:33:29.297
That's enough, you'll
scare my girl away.


00:33:34.298 --> 00:33:36.858
- I think we'll take my car after all.
- Why?


00:33:39.698 --> 00:33:43.087
I don't think my board and Narcisa's
skis will fit inside your car.


00:33:43.897 --> 00:33:46.252
Oh, come on. We'll cram them
in the top trunk.


00:33:46.657 --> 00:33:48.170
I don't know, we'll see.


00:33:48.377 --> 00:33:50.095
Suit yourselves...


00:33:50.417 --> 00:33:53.375
We could've both driven
and not stop till Salzburg.


00:33:54.177 --> 00:33:58.852
I wanted to go to Turda for New Year'
have my folks meet Cristi.


00:34:00.056 --> 00:34:03.571
So we'd rather leave straight
from there on the 3rd, luggage and all.


00:34:07.376 --> 00:34:10.890
Cristi says it's a bit early
for introductions. But...


00:34:11.215 --> 00:34:14.969
Oh, now! Let your folks see
what a dependable fellow he is.


00:34:15.655 --> 00:34:17.327
Paulie, you'd better behave...


00:34:18.255 --> 00:34:20.007
- Are you from Turda?
- Yes.


00:34:21.415 --> 00:34:23.724
- You can come, too, if you want to.
- No...


00:34:23.935 --> 00:34:27.893
- We've got the little girl...
- It's complicated...


00:34:28.574 --> 00:34:30.849
- The salmon pasta?
- For the young lady.


00:34:35.414 --> 00:34:37.974
- Where's the toilet?
- Round the corner and up the stairs.


00:34:47.133 --> 00:34:49.124
Hey, how are you?
I've called before.


00:34:51.853 --> 00:34:53.649
I know. I'm really sorry,


00:34:53.972 --> 00:34:55.883
but there was no way
I could've avoided it.


00:34:59.612 --> 00:35:00.931
I know what you mean...


00:35:04.132 --> 00:35:05.531
Oh, come on...


00:35:05.852 --> 00:35:08.365
I'm well aware that it bothers you,
try as you might to...


00:35:10.891 --> 00:35:13.928
Raluca, what are we talking about?
I'm not trying to excuse myself.


00:35:14.131 --> 00:35:15.769
Because I have no reason
to excuse myself


00:35:15.971 --> 00:35:18.883
I just wanted to tell you that
I felt like crap, too. That's it.


00:35:20.251 --> 00:35:21.968
Because I was the one who...


00:35:24.970 --> 00:35:26.244
Are you on your way right now?


00:35:26.850 --> 00:35:29.205
Oh, I'm sorry.
Should I call you back later?


00:35:33.970 --> 00:35:37.006
All right, then. As you wish.
We'll talk when you get back.


00:35:40.369 --> 00:35:41.597
Bye...


00:36:14.687 --> 00:36:17.678
You can turn it up,
I'm basically not sleeping.


00:36:30.566 --> 00:36:32.601
Humor me with a little massage?


00:36:33.925 --> 00:36:35.125
Sure.


00:36:51.604 --> 00:36:53.356
What are you doing tomorrow?


00:36:55.324 --> 00:36:58.634
The Salrom case was postponed, 'cause
Mrs. Lupea wanted it that way.


00:36:59.563 --> 00:37:00.916
Lupea who?


00:37:01.523 --> 00:37:04.196
That judge I challenged this spring.


00:37:08.563 --> 00:37:10.394
I might see Cosmina.


00:37:11.683 --> 00:37:13.718
Give her a kiss from me.


00:37:15.602 --> 00:37:17.320
Aren't you going to join us?


00:37:18.442 --> 00:37:20.478
I'll be in Constanta tomorrow.


00:37:22.322 --> 00:37:24.711
What do those people want this time?
On a Saturday.


00:37:25.722 --> 00:37:27.359
They want more...


00:37:36.721 --> 00:37:38.757
God bless you.


00:37:44.200 --> 00:37:45.553
What about Mara's piano class?


00:37:46.000 --> 00:37:48.036
Wasn't that tomorrow afternoon?


00:37:49.000 --> 00:37:51.719
- The piano lesson's on Monday, Paul.
- Yeah, that's right.


00:37:59.879 --> 00:38:02.916
We need to give Mrs. Hershcovici
her money for this month, too.


00:38:04.879 --> 00:38:06.358
I'll give it to her on Monday.


00:38:14.238 --> 00:38:17.150
So how much did we pay
for the braces after all?


00:38:18.198 --> 00:38:20.837
2700, including the treatment.


00:38:23.717 --> 00:38:25.230
Did you pay for it?


00:38:26.037 --> 00:38:28.073
No. We'll pay when we get it.


00:38:30.637 --> 00:38:33.310
Never mind,
it's better to have it put in now.


00:38:34.037 --> 00:38:35.675
You were right.


00:38:38.476 --> 00:38:40.387
Oh, this is so good...


00:39:09.554 --> 00:39:12.148
How long do you think
she'll stay in the picture?


00:39:12.434 --> 00:39:13.833
Who?


00:39:14.954 --> 00:39:16.353
Narcisa...


00:39:17.194 --> 00:39:19.627
I'm giving her a month or two.
Tops.


00:39:20.913 --> 00:39:23.666
I don't know how but he's managed to
stay on good terms with all of them.


00:39:23.913 --> 00:39:26.188
Not with the last one he didn't.


00:39:26.833 --> 00:39:29.063
- They had a nasty fight.
- I didn't know that.


00:39:33.073 --> 00:39:35.347
Well, these things happen.


00:39:39.952 --> 00:39:42.910
- She's kind of pretty, little Narcisa.
- Yeah.


00:39:47.711 --> 00:39:49.463
Done, you're handsome.


00:40:06.710 --> 00:40:08.223
How are you?


00:40:08.470 --> 00:40:10.381
Well I haven't left yet.


00:40:10.710 --> 00:40:13.463
Cosmina called me to tell me to
reschedule for two o'clock.


00:40:13.750 --> 00:40:14.978
You?


00:40:15.269 --> 00:40:16.702
Well, I'm on the road.


00:40:16.909 --> 00:40:20.106
I called earlier to ask if you want
something from the supermarket.


00:40:21.589 --> 00:40:22.817
Oh, I don't know...


00:40:23.149 --> 00:40:25.060
I could pick some stuff up
on my way back.


00:40:26.669 --> 00:40:29.307
Well, I'll think about it
and text you a list.


00:40:29.708 --> 00:40:31.141
Will you be late?


00:40:31.548 --> 00:40:34.267
I don't know yet.
It's not that busy.


00:40:38.348 --> 00:40:39.747
OK...


00:40:40.708 --> 00:40:44.859
Guess what Christmas present
my sister is getting for her husband?


00:40:45.067 --> 00:40:46.295
Tell me.


00:40:46.787 --> 00:40:48.140
Hang on to your seat.


00:40:48.547 --> 00:40:50.105
I'm hanging on to the wheel.


00:40:50.867 --> 00:40:53.506
So check this out:
A 3.000 Euros telescope.


00:40:54.307 --> 00:40:55.626
A Pentax.


00:40:56.107 --> 00:40:58.859
Very nice.
Half a year's rent.


00:40:59.706 --> 00:41:01.424
I think this is just...


00:41:02.866 --> 00:41:05.744
3.330 Euros I think.
She sent the money in Belgium


00:41:05.946 --> 00:41:07.857
to my cousin.
He'll buy it there.


00:41:08.106 --> 00:41:10.222
What can you do about that...
gives you a mind-freeze.


00:41:11.745 --> 00:41:14.259
I didn't even tell her anything
about it, believe me.


00:41:15.265 --> 00:41:17.096
She won't listen anyway.


00:41:19.225 --> 00:41:22.023
He's going to spy on the women
in the neighborhood.


00:41:22.745 --> 00:41:24.258
You bet.


00:41:24.545 --> 00:41:27.183
I don't know what she thinks she'll
accomplish with these presents?


00:41:27.784 --> 00:41:29.456
To each his own...


00:41:30.424 --> 00:41:33.575
You know he's just going to buy her
another CD Box-Set.


00:41:35.184 --> 00:41:36.458
What?


00:41:37.144 --> 00:41:39.976
I said he's going to buy her
another set of music CDs.


00:41:41.263 --> 00:41:44.255
Yeah.
"Best of Italian Music".


00:41:46.063 --> 00:41:47.974
I can barely hear you?
Where are you?


00:41:48.503 --> 00:41:52.496
It's this shitty car-kit.
I'm outside Lehliu.


00:41:52.703 --> 00:41:54.818
OK.


00:41:57.422 --> 00:41:58.696
All right, bye.


00:41:58.982 --> 00:42:01.655
- C'mon, work well. Kiss.
- Kiss, bye-bye.


00:42:50.898 --> 00:42:52.217
Good afternoon, ma'am.


00:42:52.538 --> 00:42:54.210
Hello.


00:42:56.018 --> 00:42:57.576
Raluca!


00:43:01.018 --> 00:43:03.134
Come on in. I think she's in the
bathroom, taking a shower.


00:43:03.338 --> 00:43:06.488
I'm sorry to bother you. I called from
downstairs, but she didn't answer.


00:43:14.537 --> 00:43:16.448
Ralu, Mr. Hanganu is here.


00:43:20.096 --> 00:43:22.212
Come into the living room, please.


00:43:31.216 --> 00:43:33.171
- Does Ralu know you are coming?
- What was that?


00:43:33.615 --> 00:43:35.685
Raluca...
Does she know you're here?


00:43:36.255 --> 00:43:38.815
No, I wanted to surprise her.


00:44:02.733 --> 00:44:04.371
A slice of cake.


00:44:04.893 --> 00:44:06.121
Thank you.


00:44:06.813 --> 00:44:09.725
- Happy belated birthday.
- Thank you.


00:44:12.773 --> 00:44:15.047
You've changed things around here.


00:44:15.932 --> 00:44:17.331
Yes.


00:44:51.810 --> 00:44:53.323
It's very good.


00:44:56.609 --> 00:44:58.964
So...
What's going on in the capital?


00:44:59.489 --> 00:45:00.763
It's crazy.


00:45:01.089 --> 00:45:04.001
It's better not to leave the house this,
time of year.


00:45:04.929 --> 00:45:06.203
If you can...


00:45:06.409 --> 00:45:08.047
But can you?


00:45:10.808 --> 00:45:12.127
I wanted to come to Bucharest too.


00:45:12.488 --> 00:45:15.241
Ralu insisted to come home instead.


00:45:15.808 --> 00:45:17.036
That's right.


00:45:17.328 --> 00:45:19.796
She really wanted to be here for
your birthday.


00:45:20.768 --> 00:45:22.998
I was talking about the holidays
just now.


00:45:24.767 --> 00:45:26.120
True.


00:45:31.967 --> 00:45:35.323
How's your little girl?
I heard she's a sweetheart.


00:45:38.326 --> 00:45:39.645
She is.


00:45:42.366 --> 00:45:45.244
What can you do?
We all work for our kids.


00:45:50.246 --> 00:45:52.713
You should know that I care
a lot about Raluca.


00:45:56.925 --> 00:46:01.396
We see these things differently.
If you don't mind me saying so.


00:46:01.645 --> 00:46:03.875
I don't mind. I just wanted
to tell you this.


00:46:08.444 --> 00:46:10.799
Excuse me,
I have something on the stove.


00:46:53.321 --> 00:46:56.199
- What is it with you here?
- I came to see you.


00:46:56.521 --> 00:46:57.795
Why?


00:46:58.481 --> 00:47:00.073
I wanted to see you.


00:47:00.681 --> 00:47:03.478
We said we'd see each other on
Tuesday. Has anything happened?


00:47:05.680 --> 00:47:08.035
No, I just wanted to surprise you.


00:47:08.560 --> 00:47:10.232
I'm sorry you're not happy about it.


00:47:10.520 --> 00:47:12.238
Of course I'm happy about it.


00:47:14.600 --> 00:47:16.237
Are you?


00:47:17.119 --> 00:47:18.837
I'm happy.


00:47:20.799 --> 00:47:23.950
- Did you cut your hair?
- I had it fixed up a bit.


00:47:25.599 --> 00:47:27.874
I liked it when it was
a bit longer, too.


00:47:29.399 --> 00:47:31.036
You'll get used to it.


00:47:31.678 --> 00:47:34.272
You're always getting nasty,
about new things.


00:47:37.958 --> 00:47:41.234
I called you to tell you
Mr. Hanganu was here.


00:47:41.958 --> 00:47:43.868
Still going out?


00:47:44.397 --> 00:47:46.991
I think so. I don't know
right now.


00:47:55.077 --> 00:47:56.749
Let's go to my room.


00:48:02.956 --> 00:48:05.265
I open them, she closes them.


00:48:19.795 --> 00:48:22.309
Leave Dori alone.
What have, you got against him?


00:48:27.954 --> 00:48:31.583
- How long will you stay?
- I you want me to go, tell me.


00:48:32.474 --> 00:48:35.034
I'm asking because
I'd like us to talk.


00:48:35.474 --> 00:48:37.942
OK, let's talk.


00:48:38.434 --> 00:48:40.947
That's why I told you on the phone
that I was coming back to Bucharest.


00:48:41.993 --> 00:48:44.905
Well what was I supposed to do?
I couldn't stand being without you.


00:48:45.553 --> 00:48:48.021
I've seen you,
now I can be on my way.


00:48:49.993 --> 00:48:52.268
Where are you really right now?


00:48:52.873 --> 00:48:54.271
What do you mean?


00:48:54.752 --> 00:48:56.788
Where did you tell
the family you were?


00:48:58.672 --> 00:49:00.867
I'm in Constanta.


00:49:02.592 --> 00:49:04.901
Don't worry she hasn't figured it out.


00:49:05.632 --> 00:49:07.826
And you think that's reassuring?


00:49:10.911 --> 00:49:13.744
If you stay here overnight,
she's going to figure it out.


00:49:28.590 --> 00:49:31.104
- Where did you find it?
- That's for me to know.


00:49:39.869 --> 00:49:42.178
It's just like that one.


00:50:08.067 --> 00:50:10.501
- She'd fed you cake.
- Yes.


00:50:16.907 --> 00:50:19.659
I have been tossing and turning.


00:50:21.026 --> 00:50:22.425
Me, too.


00:50:23.226 --> 00:50:24.500
On a slow fire.


00:50:24.946 --> 00:50:27.460
And I heard that upset voice
of yours over the phone, too.


00:50:27.986 --> 00:50:30.295
Then you got me the watch,
to appease me.


00:50:33.105 --> 00:50:35.221
Not true. I've got it a while back.


00:50:36.745 --> 00:50:38.064
You got it...


00:50:38.425 --> 00:50:40.336
Because you knew
the time would come.


00:50:40.625 --> 00:50:43.093
- Such far sighted man.
- Not really.


00:50:43.305 --> 00:50:45.421
For example, I forgot
about your mother.


00:50:46.544 --> 00:50:48.694
- Good thing you didn't get her flowers.
- You think?


00:50:49.264 --> 00:50:51.175
Maybe that would’ve softened
her up to me.


00:50:52.024 --> 00:50:54.174
- She gave you a hard time?
- Yep.


00:50:55.344 --> 00:50:57.494
What can you do?
She's awfully fond of you.


00:50:59.943 --> 00:51:02.855
You do realize they had
big plans for me.


00:51:03.543 --> 00:51:04.771
How about yourself?


00:51:06.503 --> 00:51:07.902
What about me?


00:51:08.223 --> 00:51:10.134
What plans do you have for yourself?


00:51:13.823 --> 00:51:17.497
Paul, I love you and I care about you
very much. Those are my plans.


00:51:19.422 --> 00:51:21.538
Approved.


00:51:24.222 --> 00:51:28.294
Of course I was taken a back by that
close encounter of the third kind.


00:51:29.381 --> 00:51:31.212
It kind of hurt me.


00:51:35.101 --> 00:51:37.376
Yesterday,
I was determined to end it.


00:51:37.581 --> 00:51:39.219
But you didn't.


00:51:40.141 --> 00:51:44.577
I cried all night long like an idiot,
and I kept thinking about what to do.


00:51:49.420 --> 00:51:51.138
Paula, Paula...


00:51:53.300 --> 00:51:55.973
You've turned me into a weakling.


00:51:58.339 --> 00:51:59.658
Me too...


00:52:00.099 --> 00:52:02.010
I haven't been getting any
peace of mind either.


00:52:03.219 --> 00:52:05.335
And now you feel better?


00:52:06.899 --> 00:52:08.218
That's good...


00:52:12.978 --> 00:52:15.333
I don't want to go through this
it ever again.


00:52:17.538 --> 00:52:19.733
I know you don't want either...


00:52:20.098 --> 00:52:22.612
But believe me, I don't handle
this things well.


00:52:26.897 --> 00:52:30.094
I'm your lover, your Constanta client
I'm whatever you want me to be.


00:52:30.737 --> 00:52:32.967
I try not to think about the other
woman in you life...


00:52:33.217 --> 00:52:35.777
...but it's hard for me when I see her.


00:52:39.496 --> 00:52:41.214
Yeah, I know.


00:52:42.016 --> 00:52:43.927
I love you very much, believe me.


00:52:44.936 --> 00:52:48.053
I don't want to hurt you.
That's the last thing I want.


00:53:09.454 --> 00:53:12.366
It would've been so great
if we’d met ten years ago.


00:53:14.214 --> 00:53:16.011
You were underage back then.


00:53:19.974 --> 00:53:21.884
Eight years ago, then.


00:53:33.493 --> 00:53:36.848
- Does it have ringtones?
- I don't think so.


00:53:39.732 --> 00:53:41.245
Is the time set?


00:53:41.772 --> 00:53:43.490
Yeah, I put in the batteries.


00:53:51.811 --> 00:53:54.450
Mita is coming by to take me
out to eat at "On Plonge"...


00:53:55.091 --> 00:53:57.207
Call her and tell her you'll be late.


00:53:57.571 --> 00:53:58.924
Can't.


00:54:00.291 --> 00:54:02.804
- You come with us, too.
- I can't.


00:54:05.330 --> 00:54:07.560
Have you made up your mind?
When are you coming back?


00:54:07.810 --> 00:54:09.038
On Tuesday.


00:54:16.369 --> 00:54:17.927
Thirty-six times.


00:54:18.249 --> 00:54:20.922
- Ask Paul if you don't believe me.
- What?


00:54:21.129 --> 00:54:24.007
How many times has Madalina
seen "The Hours"?


00:54:24.289 --> 00:54:27.122
- Come again?
- I'm talking about Madi and that movie.


00:54:27.769 --> 00:54:30.521
Oh. A whole lot of times.
What's up Cosmina?


00:54:31.728 --> 00:54:33.958
Just getting ready to head home.


00:54:34.768 --> 00:54:36.998
What are you doing, Paul?
Working on Christmas Eve, too?


00:54:37.288 --> 00:54:39.199
Aren't does banks going to close
down already?


00:54:41.488 --> 00:54:43.797
They forgot to ask
for your permission.


00:54:44.727 --> 00:54:46.922
If you’d come home earlier,
we'd have eaten together.


00:54:47.247 --> 00:54:48.726
I ate at Mc Donald's.


00:54:53.447 --> 00:54:55.915
Cosmina got a really pretty
cap for Mara.


00:54:56.607 --> 00:54:57.835
Thanks.


00:54:58.806 --> 00:55:01.445
Board, gloves, cap...


00:55:02.646 --> 00:55:05.240
-... full gear.
- It's no big deal.


00:55:05.446 --> 00:55:08.324
I just liked it 'cause it
had a tassel and strings.


00:55:08.806 --> 00:55:11.445
Wouldn't you rather show it to me
than describe it?


00:55:11.766 --> 00:55:13.835
It's on the couch.
I'll bring it to you.


00:55:14.805 --> 00:55:17.114
I heard you bought Liviu
a spy glass.


00:55:17.605 --> 00:55:20.244
It's a telescope, love. He's been
wanting it for a whole year.


00:55:20.805 --> 00:55:22.921
Oh, it's gift wrapped.
Never mind don't open it.


00:55:23.565 --> 00:55:26.715
So that's the trick? If one craves
for something for a year,


00:55:26.964 --> 00:55:28.477
the wife gets it.


00:55:28.844 --> 00:55:30.197
Oh, it's not like that, really.


00:55:30.484 --> 00:55:33.317
If you don't speak your mind
you don't get anything.


00:55:33.604 --> 00:55:35.515
For instance, I didn't
buy you anything.


00:55:36.964 --> 00:55:40.115
From our side, we got you
a blouse, two sizes smaller.


00:55:40.643 --> 00:55:43.077
You said you wanted
to shave some kilos off.


00:55:43.363 --> 00:55:44.591
You're such a sweetheart.


00:55:44.963 --> 00:55:48.114
Maybe we could all get together after
Christmas and swap presents then.


00:55:50.163 --> 00:55:52.358
- Where are you spending it?
- At Liviu's folks'.


00:55:52.763 --> 00:55:55.196
Did you fix things so that they'd send
the telescope to Breaza?


00:55:55.802 --> 00:55:57.952
How are you shipping it in, by DHL,
By UPS?


00:55:58.522 --> 00:56:00.035
Oh, you so get on my nerves.


00:56:00.562 --> 00:56:04.601
- He's just acting all tough.
- Oh. We're well acquainted.


00:56:05.322 --> 00:56:07.438
Well what shall I wish you?
Merry Christmas...


00:56:07.642 --> 00:56:10.678
And maybe we'll get to see
more of each other next year.


00:56:10.881 --> 00:56:12.155
- Sure!
- Great!


00:56:13.201 --> 00:56:15.112
Come on, let me kiss you, too.


00:56:16.921 --> 00:56:19.037
Give the astronomer a kiss, too.


00:56:22.400 --> 00:56:24.311
Let's all have a better year...


00:56:24.640 --> 00:56:26.551
Let's both be happier.
And more loved...


00:56:27.560 --> 00:56:30.074
That's right.
Thanks for the treat...


00:56:30.400 --> 00:56:32.231
...as your mother likes to say.


00:56:32.440 --> 00:56:34.078
- Bye.
- Kiss-kiss.


00:56:38.759 --> 00:56:41.956
Didn't I tell you I was
keeping the blouse for myself?


00:56:42.239 --> 00:56:43.513
No.


00:56:43.759 --> 00:56:46.592
Now I'm going to have to look for a
bigger one.


00:56:47.839 --> 00:56:49.716
I'm punishing you.
You're going with me.


00:56:53.558 --> 00:56:57.028
- What, are you crabby?
- No, I'm just tired.


00:56:57.238 --> 00:56:59.308
Well you can relax now.


00:57:13.357 --> 00:57:14.631
Dad!


00:57:16.437 --> 00:57:17.995
Dad!


00:57:54.274 --> 00:57:55.912
Mom said we should
get a smaller one,


00:57:56.194 --> 00:57:57.991
since we end up throwing
it away anyway.


00:57:58.274 --> 00:58:00.628
I said, listen, Ica, we're not
getting it for ourselves,


00:58:00.833 --> 00:58:03.108
it's for the little one.
She will enjoy it.


00:58:03.473 --> 00:58:06.033
Never mind, we know who we're
dealing with here.


00:58:07.553 --> 00:58:09.191
Same thing about the presents, too.


00:58:09.553 --> 00:58:10.872
I thought I made myself
crystal clear.


00:58:11.153 --> 00:58:12.950
We're already decided that Sant
was bringing her only a snowboard.


00:58:13.273 --> 00:58:14.546
It was more than enough.


00:58:14.752 --> 00:58:18.142
- Yeah, so?
- So what's with the synthesizer?


00:58:20.192 --> 00:58:22.990
It's a Casio, it's very good.
She can use it to practice at home.


00:58:23.752 --> 00:58:25.231
Yeah, you buy her all sorts of junk


00:58:25.432 --> 00:58:27.263
and then wonder why she's
got an attitude.


00:58:28.391 --> 00:58:30.063
It was my pleasure...


00:58:30.591 --> 00:58:32.149
In that case,
please excuse me, Dad.


00:58:34.191 --> 00:58:36.580
- So, is this one Dutch?
- It's from Denmark.


00:58:42.470 --> 00:58:44.062
Watch out,
you're whistling again...


00:58:44.350 --> 00:58:45.624
You're imagining things.


00:58:46.990 --> 00:58:49.265
Look, mother asked me
to ask you...


00:58:49.510 --> 00:58:51.546
We were thinking to get Adriana...


00:58:52.430 --> 00:58:54.739
...a purse, for Christmas.


00:58:55.750 --> 00:58:57.102
That would be swell.


00:58:57.309 --> 00:59:00.540
Stop pulling those faces!
What were we supposed to get her?


00:59:01.029 --> 00:59:02.257
A pair of boots...


00:59:02.629 --> 00:59:03.903
You're being an ass.


00:59:05.869 --> 00:59:08.747
- How much will that be?
- The gentleman already paid for it.


00:59:10.508 --> 00:59:12.863
- Happy holidays!
- Merry Christmas.


00:59:15.228 --> 00:59:18.618
- Leave it to me.
- I can help you, still...


00:59:19.828 --> 00:59:21.500
No, nothing's come up so far.


00:59:23.708 --> 00:59:25.140
Nothing I know of, at least.


00:59:27.827 --> 00:59:29.055
On the third.


00:59:32.907 --> 00:59:34.306
At your place?


00:59:35.427 --> 00:59:37.782
Hold on, let me ask Paul.


00:59:38.466 --> 00:59:40.900
Cosmina's asking if we’re spending
New Year's with them.


00:59:44.346 --> 00:59:46.018
He says we don't know yet.


00:59:50.746 --> 00:59:52.020
Sure...


00:59:52.785 --> 00:59:54.343
I'll let you know tomorrow.


00:59:58.425 --> 01:00:00.097
I'd like that, too.


01:00:03.065 --> 01:00:05.101
What you've given it to him already?


01:00:06.105 --> 01:00:07.901
So, was he delighted?


01:00:08.784 --> 01:00:10.740
Maybe he'll discover a new galaxy.


01:00:11.104 --> 01:00:14.460
Get a load of Paul, he says maybe
he's going to discover a new galaxy.


01:00:15.664 --> 01:00:16.892
Yeah...


01:00:17.704 --> 01:00:19.262
A black hole rather,
you never know.


01:00:20.783 --> 01:00:22.739
OK, kiss-kiss, bye.


01:00:26.703 --> 01:00:28.375
Why do you do stuff like this?


01:00:29.623 --> 01:00:31.022
I'm really not up for it.


01:00:32.383 --> 01:00:34.737
So you'd rather spend it
with Cristi and Narcisa?


01:00:35.182 --> 01:00:36.456
No.


01:00:37.302 --> 01:00:39.452
Then we'll stay at home with Mara.


01:00:40.222 --> 01:00:42.213
Great. Whatever you want.


01:00:45.142 --> 01:00:47.053
What's up with you, love?


01:00:47.542 --> 01:00:48.815
Nothing.


01:00:50.861 --> 01:00:54.695
You're lying to me, I know it.
Look how tense you are.


01:00:55.341 --> 01:00:57.218
It's as if you’ve swallowed
a coat hanger.


01:01:37.738 --> 01:01:39.569
I'm very much in love.


01:01:44.418 --> 01:01:46.453
I've met someone.


01:01:47.257 --> 01:01:48.895
I'm very sorry...


01:01:55.697 --> 01:01:58.131
- Oh, so that was it?
- Yes.


01:01:59.176 --> 01:02:01.565
I'm very sorry, I wanted to tell you
a long time ago, but I couldn't.


01:02:03.536 --> 01:02:05.413
So why are you telling me this now?


01:02:05.896 --> 01:02:08.615
I kept hoping I'd get over it.
I didn't think it was serious, but...


01:02:09.136 --> 01:02:10.615
I didn't get over it.


01:02:50.213 --> 01:02:52.090
So, the time for this has come, too.


01:02:52.453 --> 01:02:54.330
It could've never come.


01:02:55.132 --> 01:02:56.804
Cut the crap, will you?


01:02:57.652 --> 01:03:00.212
It couldn't not have come
'cause, it has...


01:03:00.452 --> 01:03:02.124
Not even I know how.


01:03:13.971 --> 01:03:15.199
Yes...


01:03:17.411 --> 01:03:19.163
The whole situation changes.


01:03:27.330 --> 01:03:29.366
This woman,
she's younger, isn't she?


01:03:29.570 --> 01:03:31.640
No, she's 26 years old. 27...


01:03:33.010 --> 01:03:35.763
So, you eventually found
yourself a younger one.


01:03:37.649 --> 01:03:39.082
Really ugly stuff.


01:03:45.169 --> 01:03:46.841
You're a huge disappointment to me.


01:03:49.969 --> 01:03:52.004
You're my biggest
disappointment ever...


01:04:10.647 --> 01:04:11.875
Yes...


01:04:14.167 --> 01:04:15.839
I already got them.


01:04:20.966 --> 01:04:22.558
On Sunday, yes.


01:04:24.846 --> 01:04:27.041
Sunday around noon, for lunch.


01:04:30.286 --> 01:04:31.486
OK then...


01:05:15.682 --> 01:05:17.434
So this is it, then...


01:05:18.842 --> 01:05:21.402
"You mind the home, you idiot",


01:05:21.602 --> 01:05:23.513
"while I go out gallivanting
around town".


01:05:24.202 --> 01:05:25.555
It's not like that.


01:05:27.722 --> 01:05:29.154
I don't know what
you were imagining.


01:05:29.521 --> 01:05:31.910
That I'd make friends with her
or that I'd turn a blind eye?


01:05:32.481 --> 01:05:34.233
I wasn't imagining anything.
How could I?


01:05:34.521 --> 01:05:36.000
That's why I told you.


01:05:36.401 --> 01:05:37.754
But you did want it.


01:05:37.961 --> 01:05:39.872
There's no way I could've wanted
anything like this.


01:05:40.201 --> 01:05:43.192
So you didn’t want it.
You only wanted her.


01:05:43.880 --> 01:05:46.235
Adriana, I'm aware there
can be no other way.


01:05:46.880 --> 01:05:48.154
Why not?


01:05:49.360 --> 01:05:52.477
There are women witch don't make a
big fuss if the husband is cheating.


01:05:53.800 --> 01:05:55.279
Is that what you were imagining?


01:05:55.520 --> 01:05:57.828
I wasn't imagining anything,
that's why I confessed.


01:05:58.039 --> 01:05:59.757
It seems fair to me like this.


01:06:01.039 --> 01:06:03.394
So what, now you're expecting me
to congratulate you for being fair?


01:06:05.039 --> 01:06:07.997
Good job, Paul, thank you for
telling me and for ruining my life.


01:06:08.799 --> 01:06:10.198
Adriana, please...


01:06:10.519 --> 01:06:12.748
You've ruined my life.
What, did I say something wrong?


01:06:14.358 --> 01:06:16.269
What are you pleading
with me for, now?


01:06:18.878 --> 01:06:21.187
I'm asking you to understand
that I'm shattered, too.


01:06:21.598 --> 01:06:23.270
I'm torn to pieces right now.


01:06:24.238 --> 01:06:25.511
Really?


01:06:26.317 --> 01:06:28.228
Why are you so torn?


01:06:29.357 --> 01:06:31.427
Because I don’t want to hurt you.


01:06:32.437 --> 01:06:34.553
And because I am very well aware
of what I am losing.


01:06:35.357 --> 01:06:36.790
Amazing!


01:06:38.037 --> 01:06:40.152
You're still the one
playing the victim.


01:06:41.036 --> 01:06:42.310
No, I'm not.


01:06:42.556 --> 01:06:44.308
Aren't you ashamed of yourself?


01:06:44.836 --> 01:06:46.872
Why are you putting on
the sad show here with me?


01:06:48.876 --> 01:06:50.832
You're awfully lame, you know.


01:06:51.356 --> 01:06:52.947
OK, I'm lame.


01:06:57.315 --> 01:06:58.953
I told you I was sorry.


01:06:59.315 --> 01:07:01.783
Do you want me to poke one of
my eyes out so you believe me?


01:07:02.035 --> 01:07:04.503
What can I do now?
I can't pretend it never happened.


01:07:11.794 --> 01:07:13.546
Let me see you telling Mara...


01:07:13.754 --> 01:07:16.188
...that her father and her mother
are not together anymore.


01:07:16.914 --> 01:07:18.427
We'll tell her together.


01:07:19.554 --> 01:07:21.669
We're not doing anything
together anymore, Paul.


01:07:23.153 --> 01:07:25.872
The instant you're with another
woman, you're no longer here.


01:07:26.473 --> 01:07:28.145
We don't do stuff together.


01:07:29.393 --> 01:07:32.430
'Cause we didn't sleep with
another woman together.


01:07:34.193 --> 01:07:36.547
Or, what,
you didn't sleep with her?


01:07:38.392 --> 01:07:40.508
OK, then. I'll tell her myself.


01:07:42.832 --> 01:07:44.470
That her father no longer...


01:07:49.511 --> 01:07:53.743
That daddy loves another woman
and that he can't live without her.


01:07:54.231 --> 01:07:55.459
Right?


01:07:55.791 --> 01:07:57.861
Please understand. It just happened.


01:07:58.551 --> 01:08:00.030
It's not something I wanted.


01:08:00.351 --> 01:08:01.830
Aren't you ashamed of yourself?


01:08:02.031 --> 01:08:05.579
It's never happened to me!
I don't fuck married men.


01:08:05.830 --> 01:08:07.502
I feel like bashing my head
against this heater,


01:08:07.750 --> 01:08:09.945
for wasting my life with you.


01:08:10.670 --> 01:08:13.184
- You never loved me.
- I did love you.


01:08:13.870 --> 01:08:16.065
I know it sounds shitty,
but it's true.


01:08:16.670 --> 01:08:18.387
It sounds really shitty, Paul.


01:08:20.389 --> 01:08:22.505
If you loved me, you wouldn't
have broken our home.


01:08:22.709 --> 01:08:24.859
You have a child, a family
and you two just shit on them!


01:08:25.069 --> 01:08:26.548
You and that woman!


01:08:28.349 --> 01:08:30.783
And now you're acting all
super-wise and shit with me...


01:08:31.948 --> 01:08:34.621
Please, do calm down. You're only
making it worse for yourself.


01:08:35.028 --> 01:08:37.144
Worse how, Paul?


01:08:38.068 --> 01:08:41.504
- What could be worse than this?
- You're making it worse.


01:08:58.627 --> 01:09:00.025
You fucking jerk!


01:09:45.903 --> 01:09:48.337
Tell me, how long have you been
taking me for an idiot?


01:09:49.783 --> 01:09:52.616
I just want you to tell for how long
have you been cheating on me?


01:09:53.623 --> 01:09:57.137
- A few months.
- I see. How many months?


01:09:57.902 --> 01:09:59.130
Nearly five.


01:09:59.422 --> 01:10:02.539
- Since when, precisely?
- Since five months ago.


01:10:03.422 --> 01:10:04.855
Since August.


01:10:05.702 --> 01:10:07.135
Since July!


01:10:09.621 --> 01:10:11.293
What were we doing in July?


01:10:14.941 --> 01:10:16.260
Who is she?


01:10:17.941 --> 01:10:19.260
It's Raluca.


01:10:19.861 --> 01:10:21.260
Raluca who?


01:10:22.621 --> 01:10:24.133
The dentist.


01:10:25.940 --> 01:10:28.454
Is she the one with braces,
the one we took Mara to?


01:10:30.380 --> 01:10:33.019
You took the child to have her
work on her mouth.


01:10:34.380 --> 01:10:36.416
So what did you tell her?
Did you introduce them?


01:10:36.660 --> 01:10:38.456
"Mara, here's your next mommy. "


01:10:38.979 --> 01:10:41.812
Cut it out!
I didn't tell Mara anything.


01:10:42.099 --> 01:10:44.852
You're a liar and a sleaze and you
had her work on the child's mouth,


01:10:45.059 --> 01:10:47.493
with the same hands with which
she gives you hand-jobs.


01:10:48.259 --> 01:10:50.136
That's who you are!


01:10:50.339 --> 01:10:52.693
What you're saying right now
is sleazier and uglier than that.


01:10:59.698 --> 01:11:01.051
Raluca...


01:11:03.938 --> 01:11:06.326
How she stood there,
telling me about those braces...


01:11:07.737 --> 01:11:09.250
Amazing...


01:11:11.337 --> 01:11:13.407
And I just stood there
like an idiot, listening to her.


01:11:16.097 --> 01:11:18.292
With the child on the dentist chair.


01:11:22.896 --> 01:11:25.569
How does this girl know
what's best for my child?


01:11:26.416 --> 01:11:27.769
What do you mean?


01:11:28.976 --> 01:11:31.171
You two aren't going
to make her wear any braces.


01:11:31.376 --> 01:11:33.331
What do you mean?
That's her job.


01:11:33.535 --> 01:11:35.526
Mara has a problem and
it needs to be taken care of.


01:11:35.735 --> 01:11:38.169
So where did she get the money
to start that clinic of hers?


01:11:38.375 --> 01:11:39.694
Oh, give me a break with that crap!


01:11:39.895 --> 01:11:41.533
I am not cutting anything out, Paul!


01:11:41.735 --> 01:11:43.930
I have the right to know, don't I?


01:11:44.135 --> 01:11:45.807
I have the right to know
who you're fucking!


01:11:46.055 --> 01:11:49.171
Well, then, ask me and I'll answer.
What do you want to know?


01:11:52.014 --> 01:11:53.527
Give her a call, Paul.


01:11:54.534 --> 01:11:56.252
Call her and tell her I found out.


01:11:56.654 --> 01:11:58.451
She doesn't have to play
the fool anymore.


01:11:59.294 --> 01:12:00.568
Call her!


01:12:02.133 --> 01:12:03.486
Why aren't you calling her?


01:12:03.853 --> 01:12:05.525
Call her, tell her I know.


01:12:06.133 --> 01:12:08.693
- Where's that phone?
- Come on, cut it out...


01:12:09.293 --> 01:12:10.692
What's her name?


01:12:11.133 --> 01:12:12.361
Raluca.


01:12:12.973 --> 01:12:14.292
Ralu-caca.


01:12:14.613 --> 01:12:17.001
Where's the R key
on this shitty phone?


01:12:17.452 --> 01:12:19.761
- Fuck you and your Raluca.
- Give me the damn phone!


01:12:20.092 --> 01:12:21.764
Call her, Paul.


01:12:22.572 --> 01:12:24.244
Call her to tell her I found out.


01:12:25.292 --> 01:12:27.248
- I will.
- That's right, great!


01:12:29.531 --> 01:12:33.285
Or did you lie to her, too?
Does she know that you're married?


01:12:34.891 --> 01:12:37.724
You know I didn't lie to her.
She knows that I'm married.


01:12:38.331 --> 01:12:40.242
So she's talked you into
leaving your family.


01:12:40.651 --> 01:12:43.289
On the contrary.
She's never even alluded to it.


01:12:45.610 --> 01:12:47.805
You have such nice things
to say about her.


01:12:48.410 --> 01:12:50.082
See, I'm all teary-eyed.


01:12:50.970 --> 01:12:53.279
I'm just trying to tell you that I
was the one who took this decision.


01:12:53.490 --> 01:12:55.799
She didn't pressure me in any way.


01:12:56.290 --> 01:12:57.722
Please understand that.


01:13:00.129 --> 01:13:01.403
Call her.


01:13:04.289 --> 01:13:05.688
Call her!


01:13:35.927 --> 01:13:37.406
Hi...


01:13:38.447 --> 01:13:41.404
Look, I just called to
let you know I told Adriana.


01:13:42.846 --> 01:13:45.918
You fucking retarded shit-hole!


01:13:49.486 --> 01:13:51.044
You goddamn jerk!


01:14:02.125 --> 01:14:03.444
You... Let me go!


01:14:08.604 --> 01:14:10.162
Let me go...


01:14:20.804 --> 01:14:22.202
Let me go...


01:14:56.921 --> 01:14:59.310
I want you to leave.


01:15:01.841 --> 01:15:03.512
Go wherever you best see fit.


01:15:07.840 --> 01:15:09.751
That's just what I need to do.


01:16:58.112 --> 01:17:00.148
May I please have my keys?


01:17:21.431 --> 01:17:24.228
Don't think you're taking my child
away from me, Paul.


01:17:33.190 --> 01:17:35.579
I'll make sure you never
see the child again.


01:17:37.629 --> 01:17:40.063
Have that girl make you one herself.


01:17:41.189 --> 01:17:43.259
I don't know if that’s what I want.


01:21:09.174 --> 01:21:10.573
Hey, how are you?


01:21:11.014 --> 01:21:12.732
I just got here.


01:21:15.294 --> 01:21:17.603
No, it doesn't seem cold.


01:21:21.254 --> 01:21:24.450
She wasn't there but she does know
I've started to move my stuff out.


01:21:27.613 --> 01:21:28.887
OK.


01:21:33.413 --> 01:21:35.972
Did you already promise you'd go?


01:21:37.532 --> 01:21:38.806
I see.


01:21:40.452 --> 01:21:43.649
No, 'cause I need to go see her,
and Mara, and my folks, too.


01:21:45.772 --> 01:21:48.411
Can I throw away the coffee
in that polka-dot tin?


01:21:50.251 --> 01:21:53.004
What do you mean you don't own one
if I'm holding it right now.


01:21:55.331 --> 01:21:58.243
White, with some colored dots...


01:22:01.731 --> 01:22:04.085
I thought it was just
some stale coffee.


01:22:04.930 --> 01:22:06.886
Never mind, I'll put it
somewhere else.


01:22:09.970 --> 01:22:11.688
I have to get the door for Cristi.


01:22:12.890 --> 01:22:14.608
He's helping me assemble the locker.


01:22:15.490 --> 01:22:17.128
Yeah, I bought it.


01:22:20.089 --> 01:22:21.807
What was that?


01:22:22.449 --> 01:22:25.521
Same as the other one.
Maybe in a slightly lighter shade.


01:22:28.329 --> 01:22:29.967
Shall I put them up on the shelves?


01:22:33.248 --> 01:22:34.567
Hold on a second.


01:22:46.207 --> 01:22:47.435
So...


01:22:48.647 --> 01:22:50.160
Raluca says hello.


01:22:50.607 --> 01:22:53.519
Hello... Ask her why
she doesn't have a Christmas tree.


01:22:53.727 --> 01:22:55.160
You heard that?


01:22:55.447 --> 01:22:57.915
She says you can buy one for her.


01:23:01.766 --> 01:23:04.838
Listen, there's no point in me
clearing up room for clothes.


01:23:05.046 --> 01:23:07.276
I think the best way is to let you
arrange things when you get back.


01:23:08.686 --> 01:23:10.085
All right.


01:23:11.806 --> 01:23:13.285
Well, I don't know.


01:23:14.045 --> 01:23:16.161
If you head out here before lunch,
you'll catch me.


01:23:16.365 --> 01:23:19.118
I have to be at my folks' around six.


01:23:21.125 --> 01:23:22.558
The day after tomorrow?


01:23:24.885 --> 01:23:26.841
I thought it was going
to be tomorrow.


01:23:28.004 --> 01:23:31.121
No, there's no problem.
You come back whenever you can.


01:23:35.284 --> 01:23:36.797
We'll talk around ten.


01:23:38.844 --> 01:23:41.153
After your mom goes to sleep, yeah.


01:23:42.643 --> 01:23:44.235
Come on. Bye. Bye.


01:23:45.883 --> 01:23:47.475
Throw a beer my way, man.


01:24:03.042 --> 01:24:04.953
"12:08 East Of Bucharest"


01:24:05.162 --> 01:24:07.232
She got this one
at Carturesti Store.


01:24:07.722 --> 01:24:09.713
- Could be.
- For sure.


01:24:16.441 --> 01:24:17.794
Cheers.


01:24:31.880 --> 01:24:34.189
It's done up pretty nicely,
but it's kind of small.


01:24:34.960 --> 01:24:36.439
Well, now...


01:24:37.200 --> 01:24:39.155
With the both of you living here...


01:24:40.319 --> 01:24:42.355
- Yeah.
- Well, yeah.


01:24:49.079 --> 01:24:52.070
As they say, the New Year
brought a change in your life.


01:24:52.958 --> 01:24:54.710
Are we going to start putting
that locker together?


01:24:55.238 --> 01:24:58.150
Let's finish our beers first,
relax a little.


01:25:21.076 --> 01:25:23.715
- Adriana is not with you?
- I thought she'd be here by now.


01:25:23.996 --> 01:25:26.351
When I talked to her
she was around Mosilor Street.


01:25:26.756 --> 01:25:29.589
- Nucu! Let's set the table.
- Of course we will.


01:25:29.796 --> 01:25:31.593
Come on, Mara, help me out, too.


01:25:35.155 --> 01:25:37.305
- How are you, Dad?
- Fine, honey.


01:25:37.515 --> 01:25:39.346
Are you setting the table?


01:25:40.355 --> 01:25:42.027
She's helping me out.


01:25:42.235 --> 01:25:43.714
How are you?


01:25:43.915 --> 01:25:45.234
- All by yourself?
- Adriana's going to be here soon.


01:25:45.435 --> 01:25:48.107
-Daddy do you want to see what I got?
- Show me!


01:25:49.274 --> 01:25:51.151
I hope she hasn't found the presents.


01:25:51.514 --> 01:25:54.267
Olguta came by yesterday
and she didn't come empty-handed.


01:26:02.513 --> 01:26:04.231
Look what I got!


01:26:07.833 --> 01:26:09.789
Wow, that's so neat.


01:26:10.313 --> 01:26:12.463
- Noah's ark.
- It's not Noah's ark!


01:26:12.793 --> 01:26:15.261
It's the Barbie Party Cruiser.
See, it even has an alarm.


01:26:17.512 --> 01:26:20.663
And if you open it,
you find a disco ball.


01:26:20.912 --> 01:26:24.188
- A black Barbie?
- No, she just has a tan!


01:26:24.552 --> 01:26:27.589
- Grams, where's the bar?
- Wherever you left it, honey.


01:26:28.712 --> 01:26:29.940
Oh, yeah...


01:26:32.311 --> 01:26:33.664
Found it!


01:26:36.471 --> 01:26:38.063
Look dad, a bar!


01:26:38.271 --> 01:26:40.990
When you press this, it starts
to move. Can I have Barbie?


01:26:41.231 --> 01:26:42.505
Listen to that lisp!


01:26:42.711 --> 01:26:45.349
Why did you put those
wires on her teeth?


01:26:45.550 --> 01:26:47.620
- You're so clueless!
- Don't you talk back like that.


01:26:48.110 --> 01:26:51.022
Don't worry, Paul. Santa might
hear and decide not to come.


01:26:51.430 --> 01:26:53.341
Look, she wants to have a pizza.


01:26:53.590 --> 01:26:55.182
Feed her some.


01:26:56.870 --> 01:26:59.622
Look, she's gotten all dirty.


01:27:01.269 --> 01:27:03.339
I have Boeuf salad...


01:27:03.629 --> 01:27:06.826
...some pressed cheese
and meats for starters.


01:27:07.789 --> 01:27:10.861
For second course
some cabbage rolls.


01:27:11.069 --> 01:27:12.501
I'll take them out of the oven.


01:27:12.748 --> 01:27:15.467
You said you'd bring
a cake for dessert.


01:27:16.068 --> 01:27:17.660
I hope Adriana hasn't forgotten.


01:27:17.908 --> 01:27:20.376
I made some cookies just in case.


01:27:20.588 --> 01:27:22.818
Take a look,
you're my food critic.


01:27:23.108 --> 01:27:24.826
- Can I have one, too?
- What, honey-bunny?


01:27:25.028 --> 01:27:27.018
- A cookie.
- After dinner, baby.


01:27:27.227 --> 01:27:29.900
- But is Barbie allowed one now?
- Sure, Barbie is allowed.


01:27:31.067 --> 01:27:32.580
It's good...


01:27:32.867 --> 01:27:35.017
We have to remember to remove
the braces before dinner.


01:27:35.427 --> 01:27:37.463
OK, but what about the presents?


01:27:37.667 --> 01:27:40.226
Mother has to get here first, and
then presents will show up, too.


01:27:40.426 --> 01:27:42.417
Mother will get here first,
and then Santa will come, too.


01:27:42.626 --> 01:27:44.776
If we put the food on the table,
he'll get here faster.


01:27:48.346 --> 01:27:50.416
Call Adriana, it's getting late.


01:27:50.746 --> 01:27:52.259
Late for what?


01:27:52.506 --> 01:27:55.815
- What's she doing right now anyway?
- She's gone to buy the cake.


01:27:56.145 --> 01:27:57.976
I'm kind of hungry.


01:28:01.785 --> 01:28:03.901
Mommy's coming!
Mommy's coming!


01:28:05.105 --> 01:28:06.697
How are you, sweetheart?


01:28:07.785 --> 01:28:10.344
I was about to say how you've grown
since I last saw you.


01:28:10.744 --> 01:28:13.212
She's really changed, hasn't she?
I think she's gotten heavier.


01:28:13.424 --> 01:28:14.982
Look who’s here...


01:28:15.424 --> 01:28:17.574
Have Ica and Nucu started
you on a fattening diet?


01:28:17.784 --> 01:28:19.536
I'll take the wine
and the water now.


01:28:20.024 --> 01:28:21.343
The presents?


01:28:21.624 --> 01:28:23.022
In the pantry.


01:28:23.223 --> 01:28:24.781
Don't forget to distract her.


01:28:24.983 --> 01:28:26.974
I'll call her out on the balcony
to watch the fireworks.


01:28:27.183 --> 01:28:28.821
Mom, look!


01:28:29.623 --> 01:28:31.932
I saw it. Very nice.


01:28:32.143 --> 01:28:34.099
I fail to see what's so nice about it.


01:28:34.583 --> 01:28:37.619
It's pink, but you can't see it,
'cause it's inside.


01:28:39.822 --> 01:28:41.494
Let your mom take her coat off.


01:28:42.022 --> 01:28:43.853
But I want to show it to Mom, too.


01:28:45.822 --> 01:28:50.100
I got the Barbie Party Cruiser,
with Barbie, a bar and a pool.


01:28:50.701 --> 01:28:52.054
What did you get?


01:28:52.341 --> 01:28:54.411
A Barbie boat from Olga.


01:28:56.861 --> 01:29:00.012
Take this boat someplace else
honey, this is not playtime.


01:29:00.781 --> 01:29:03.773
Do you want Santa to find us
unprepared like this?


01:29:03.981 --> 01:29:06.210
Come on,
put it in grandma's room.


01:29:06.740 --> 01:29:09.129
Oh, don't you have
a hard-knock life?


01:29:20.779 --> 01:29:23.418
I'm not going to stay on for
too long. I'll let them know, too.


01:29:28.019 --> 01:29:31.568
- I suppose you told them already.
- No. After the holidays.


01:29:33.778 --> 01:29:36.497
Good thing you're concerned
with not ruining their joy.


01:29:37.258 --> 01:29:39.328
You want me
to tell them right now?


01:29:40.938 --> 01:29:43.930
I'd rather not tell you what
I want right now.


01:29:46.617 --> 01:29:49.848
On a completely different topic,
I'm going to go in Austria with Mara.


01:29:52.697 --> 01:29:55.165
So, you want us to tell Mara before.


01:29:56.177 --> 01:29:59.726
You'll tell her when we both
agree it's best.


01:30:01.416 --> 01:30:04.294
I don't want us to pretend that
nothing happened.


01:30:06.616 --> 01:30:09.176
But I don't want you to
traumatize her either.


01:30:12.216 --> 01:30:15.013
When she finds out,
what exactly she finds out...


01:30:15.455 --> 01:30:16.683
We'll see...


01:30:19.935 --> 01:30:22.165
So you're saying we shouldn't
call off the holiday.


01:30:24.615 --> 01:30:28.130
We, Paul, are calling off absolutely
everything concerning the two of us.


01:30:30.214 --> 01:30:32.409
If I'm going,
I'm doing it for Mara.


01:30:34.614 --> 01:30:36.650
That's what I was talking about, too.


01:30:41.774 --> 01:30:44.128
I'd better put this in a cup, right?


01:30:44.333 --> 01:30:45.686
Leave it like that.


01:30:45.973 --> 01:30:48.089
It's for the stuffed eggs.


01:30:48.373 --> 01:30:50.603
Ica! Nucu said "buzz off. "


01:30:50.813 --> 01:30:53.930
I'm going to teach
this Nucu a lesson.


01:30:54.373 --> 01:30:57.330
- Should we take out the presents now?
- We will, Mother, be patient.


01:30:57.772 --> 01:30:59.649
It's as if you were the children here...


01:30:59.972 --> 01:31:03.044
All right... You don't have to
take that tone with me.


01:31:11.051 --> 01:31:13.724
I'm going to need your written
agreement for Austria.


01:31:17.731 --> 01:31:21.519
When the divorce is final and
the Court entrusts the child to me,


01:31:21.731 --> 01:31:23.244
you won't need to do that anymore.


01:31:23.491 --> 01:31:24.843
I understand.


01:31:26.010 --> 01:31:28.046
Till then, that's where we stand.


01:31:29.810 --> 01:31:31.289
All right, then. Bottom line.


01:31:31.930 --> 01:31:34.569
Not tomorrow, nor
the day after tomorrow...


01:31:35.890 --> 01:31:37.721
Call me in the morning
of the 27'th.


01:31:37.930 --> 01:31:41.239
We'll go to the notary and
you'll issue the statement for me.


01:31:42.129 --> 01:31:44.882
And then we'll decide on what
and when you tell Mara.


01:31:45.609 --> 01:31:47.486
- All right?
- Right...


01:31:48.889 --> 01:31:50.288
Who could that be?


01:31:50.489 --> 01:31:52.286
Probably the garbage men.


01:31:54.568 --> 01:31:56.286
Who is it?


01:31:56.528 --> 01:31:58.598
It's the carolers!


01:32:06.448 --> 01:32:08.438
Paul! The presents!


01:33:00.444 --> 01:33:01.843
That's all?


01:33:02.324 --> 01:33:04.393
Do you know
"Let us praise the Lord?"


01:33:51.560 --> 01:33:55.553
Subtitling
Empire Video Production, Romania

